# Dashboard Modularization & HTML Template Reorganization

## Background

`dashboard.js` has grown to **16,104 lines / 1.04 MB** containing **137 `app.*` functions** across 20+ distinct feature domains. The dashboard `templates/` folder mixes standalone hub pages (`credit_card.html`, `trips.html`, `portal.html`, `net_worth.html`, `stock_detail.html`) with the dashboard partial system (`dashboard/` subdirectory). We need to:

1. Split `dashboard.js` into feature-scoped modules loaded as `<script>` tags.
2. Reorganize the HTML templates into a clear, hub-oriented folder hierarchy.
3. Extract reusable modal/component partials shared across hubs.

---

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Module Loading Strategy**: The current architecture injects all functions onto a **global `app` object** (no ES module `import/export`). The modularization strategy here **preserves that pattern** — each module file appends its functions to `window.app` via `app.xxx = function(){}` style, so no HTML `type="module"` or bundler is needed. This is the safe, zero-risk path.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **`_body_footer.html` contains both modal HTML and `<script>` includes.** As part of reorganization, the 609-line `_body_footer.html` will be split into:
> - `_modals.html` — all floating modals (swing range, stock rating, audit, watchlist, stock note, breakout notes)
> - `_stock_modal.html` — the full-screen stock intelligence iframe modal
> - `_script_tags.html` — the `<script src="...">` block only

