## Key Implementation Rules

1. **Module file header** (every new module must start with this):
```javascript
// =========================================================================
// [Module Name] — Nexus Dashboard Module
// Extracted from dashboard.js — modularization 2026-08-28
// =========================================================================
(function() {
    const API_BASE = window.API_BASE || window.location.origin;
    const app = window.app;
    if (!app) { console.error('[MODULE] window.app not initialized'); return; }
```

2. **Module file footer**:
```javascript
})(); // end IIFE
```

3. **No function renames** — all `app.functionName` must stay identical to avoid breaking HTML inline handlers.

4. **`BREAKOUT_COLUMNS` and `DEFAULT_BREAKOUT_COLS`** are local consts in `dashboard.js`. When extracting `modules/breakout.js`, move them to module-scope (inside the IIFE, before any functions that reference them).

5. **After each extraction from `dashboard.js`** replace the extracted block with:
```javascript
// [section name] → extracted to modules/xxx.js
```

6. **Cache busting**: Update `?v=` on all script tags to `20260828_v22_modular`.

